  designNotes: "2026-08-27, explicit user request (試試看加入 Meshy_AI_Parkside_Portrait_biped\
    \ (10).zip 這個動作，沒有指定具體用途，當成普通進攻池的第四招試\
    \ 加) - measured via AnimationMode.SampleAnimationClip (same methodology as every\
    \ other attack this session), tracking BladeHitbox position/speed relative to root\
    \ across the whole 2.53s clip. Low crouching lunge pose (screenshot-checked, not\
    \ corrupted). Damage/poise/knockback (22/16/3) and cooldown (2.2s) sit between\
    \ QuickSlash's fast-flurry tuning and OverheadSlam's heavy-hit tuning - a normal\
    \ mid-weight slash, not trying to be the fastest or hardest-hitting attack in the\
    \ pool.\n\n2026-08-27 correction, found via live in-Play testing (not just offline\
    \ sampling): the first pick for the hit window (t=0.15-0.25, the fastest/dominant\
    \ swing, peak blade speed 66.9 units/s at t=0.18) was WRONG - live-fired via\
    \ BeginAttack against the actual combat target, it never registered a hit at any\
    \ horizontal placement because that swing's absolute world height stays at\
    \ Y~2.4-3.9 for its whole duration, while the target's collider only spans\
    \ Y~0.5-1.5 (confirmed via a control test: even the already-proven-working\
    \ SwordJudgment attack only barely grazes hit height at its own lowest point\
    \ against the same target - a swing that never drops below Y=2.4 genuinely cannot\
    \ connect, full stop). Re-sampled the whole clip in absolute world Y (not just\
    \ root-relative) and found the third, previously-deprioritized \"secondary\" motion\
    \ is actually the only part of this clip that comes down to reachable height: Y\
    \ drops from 1.82 to 0.90 across t=0.79-0.97 while forward reach stays strong\
    \ (2.1-2.7 world units) - moved the hit window here instead (now 0.76-0.97). Reads\
    \ better thematically too (a lunge ending in a committed low finishing cut) than\
    \ the original overhead-style pick. First re-verify attempt was ALSO invalid for an\
    \ unrelated reason - the GameObject used as the live test dummy (\"中立者2\", found\
    \ via a PlayerCombat+Health component search) turned out not to be\
    \ BossStateMachine.target at all (a same-named-component decoy elsewhere in the\
    \ scene); real target is the GameObject literally named \"Player\". Once retested\
    \ against the correct Player object: a guaranteed-overlap pass (player teleported\
    \ onto the blade's own position every active frame) confirmed the damage pipeline\
    \ fires correctly (500 -> 478, -22 matching baseHealthDamage) at the expected\
    \ normalized time (~0.79, right at the window start). Then a realistic, non-glued\
    \ pass - player placed once at a natural 1.8-unit melee distance in front of Wushi,\
    \ facing tracking left fully live for the whole attack - ALSO landed the same -22\
    \ hit at step 100 (norm~0.79) with no cheating involved, confirming the move\
    \ connects at ordinary melee range in real gameplay conditions, not just when\
    \ forced to overlap."
